# Copilot likes tables, and Telegram has no table markup: a monospace block wraps on a
# phone into something unreadable. So a notification's tables are sent as pictures with
# the table drawn in them, each where it stood: the text before it, the picture, the
# text after. The second table here is wider than a phone and has to wrap to stay
# readable; the dump shows the order, and the pictures are in the run directory.

size 110x30
arg --mux
fake_telegram private
session existing-app Existing app session

wait_for Existing app session
press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot is idling

# What the session said: prose, a table, more prose. The stub reads \n as a line break.
type e2e:work 1500 Here are the **results**:\n\n| Name | Size | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| alpha | 12 KB | ok |\n| beta | 3 MB | failed |\n\nAnd the losses:\n\n| Specialist | Selected pass | Best development loss | Final development loss |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Generation | 2 of 5 | 0.5487 | 0.8387 |\n| Repair | 3 of 4 | 0.1125 | 0.1240 |\n\nShall I retry beta?
press enter
press ctrl+b d
wait_for Existing app session

telegram_wait Here are the <b>results</b>:
telegram_wait And the losses:
telegram_wait Shall I retry beta?
telegram_expect_not <pre>
telegram_wait photo 
telegram_expect_not picture below
telegram_expect_not cst-table
telegram_dump 01-table-sent
